    thinking: "**Conceptualizing GigBuddy Marketplace**\n\nOkay, I\'m now honing in on the core architecture for \"GigBuddy.\" I\'m currently envisioning a dual-view system, catering separately to event organizers and musicians. A global sticky toggle will manage the user\'s current perspective within the application, based on their role. I\'m excited by this approach.\n\n\n**Defining the Aesthetic Framework**\n\nI\'ve decided on \"Midnight Studio\" as the design language. I\'ve defined the color palette and background styles: dark backgrounds, high-contrast text, electric violet for CTAs, and green/amber for success/alerts. Now, I\'m analyzing the file structure within the React Vite setup to see how I can integrate the visual language. I\'ll need to define the foundational components, starting with the React dashboard.\n\n\n**Refining Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the frontend architecture, focusing on the layouts, client-side routing, and functional view states. I\'m targeting clean functional components and semantic HTML layouts, and I plan to embed mock data matching the system parameters for beautifully populated fields. I will use local storage or React state for now since a DB or backend isn\'t requested. Image generation is valuable for user avatars, musician profiles, and concert flyers. I\'ll remember this for later.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m verifying the project structure now. Examining the `package.json` dependencies suggests a potential Express backend. However, a deeper look at the file system, including `index.js`, indicates no explicit `server.ts` file or backend integration. The focus remains on frontend development, adhering to the specifications of the prompt.\n\n\n"
