  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Build Success**\n\nThe build completed without a hitch; it\'s quite the achievement! Now, I\'m focusing on crafting a succinct and informative summary of the project\'s milestones, adhering to the communication style guidelines provided. The aim is to present a clean, proportional overview of our work, highlighting key accomplishments effectively.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented the full frontend layout and core interactive state engine for **GigBuddy**\342\200\224a premium, end-to-end marketplace built specifically for live music events, designed to resemble high-end platforms like Spotify and Splice.\n\nHere is a conceptual and functional overview of what has been constructed:\n\n### \360\237\216\250 Visual & Design Identity: \"Midnight Studio\" Theme\nThe application incorporates a sleek, modern visual hierarchy engineered for entertainment and creative professionals:\n*   **Canvas & Atmosphere**: Set against an immersive deep charcoal and midnight backdrop, using structural zinc borders instead of heavy shadows for a crisp, flat editorial feel.\n*   **Typography**: Features a balanced pairing of **Space Grotesk** for display-ready headers and **JetBrains Mono** for logistical timelines, budgets, and security statuses.\n*   **Aesthetic Accents**: Integrated electric violet as the primary branding color, emerald green to signify financial security/escrow holds, and soft amber to highlight pending reviews and critical timeline rules.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\224\204 Dual-View Architecture & Interactive Flow State\nThe workspace features a global sticky sandbox switcher that allows you to swap roles instantly and test the live relationship between **Event Planners** and **Live Musicians**:\n\n#### 1. View A: Event Planners & Organizers (The Buyers)\n*   **High-Level Metric Trackers**: Monitors active open calls, pending musician applications, and confirmed bookings with real-time indicators.\n*   **Gig Sourcing Feed**: Lists all active events with live status badges. Allows planners to review candidate files and cancel unbooked events.\n*   **The Gig Creator Form**: A single-page call editor with:\n    *   **Preset Tag Selectors**: Instantly add or custom-define music genres, performance instrument slots, and on-site venue backline gear (e.g., specific drumkits, PA columns, and guitar amps).\n    *   **Live Interactive Preview**: A real-time rendering panel on the right side showing exactly how the active post appears to live musicians.\n*   **Application Review Deck**: View musician bios, specialized performance skills, and customized cover letters. Includes buttons to decline candidates or approve their profiles.\n\n#### 2. View B: Musicians & Sessionists (The Sellers)\n*   **Pipeline Summary**: Tracks upcoming booked shows, pending gigs, and projected earnings safely secured in the platform\'s escrow holding state.\n*   **Gig Marketplace Feed**: A split-pane interface:\n    *   *Left Pane*: A scrollable column displaying available open calls with genre tags and compensation badges.\n    *   *Right Pane*: Dynamically displays the detailed logistics of the selected gig (strict soundcheck times, curfew windows, provided backline, and performance rules) with a prompt to apply.\n    *   *Interactive Application Form*: Submit custom cover notes and select from multiple personal instruments to apply immediately.\n*   **Multi-Band Availability Tracker**: An interactive weekly grid that lets musicians toggle individual days of the week between *Available*, *Busy*, and *Tentative* in a single click.\n*   **Project Registry**: Create and manage a registry of active bands, duos, or orchestras you tour or perform session work with.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\234 Electronic MoA Contract Modal & Escrow Simulator\nWhen a planner approves a candidate, they draft a standard legal **Memorandum of Agreement**:\n*   Renders an official digital contract detailing soundcheck/set schedules, liability limits, and direct escrow protection clauses.\n*   Accepting the terms and typing a full legal signature officially binds the agreement\342\200\224instantly updating the candidate state to *Booked*, moving the budget into the locked secure escrow count, and transitioning the gig\'s listing state from *Sourcing* to *Confirmed*.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\225\271\357\270\217 Interactive Sandbox Tour Guide\nA step-by-step walkthrough is rendered at the bottom of the screen to guide reviewers through a complete loop: from vetting Clara Sterling\'s jazz double-bass application, signing her MoA, switching to the Live Musician role to apply for the Rock Cover Band, and switching back to Planner to finalize the contract.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 48986528
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
