  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing App Completion**\n\nThe previous tool calls were indeed successful, and linting completed without issue, alongside a clean applet compilation. Now I need to encapsulate this successful development cycle into a summary.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully architected and implemented the core frontend structure for **GigBuddy**\342\200\224a premium, legally-protective marketplace connecting event planners and gigging musicians. \n\nThe application is completely functional, fully responsive, and has successfully passed all build-compilation and TypeScript linter checks.\n\n### \360\237\214\214 Visual Design: \"Midnight Studio\"\nEvery visual accent reflects a high-end SaaS dashboard built for the modern entertainment industry (reminiscent of premium audio platforms like Spotify or Splice):\n* **Deep Monochromatic Canvas:** Grounded with a deep dark `bg-zinc-950` body, `bg-zinc-900` containers, and clean `border-zinc-800` borders.\n* **Premium Typography:** Anchored with high-contrast, energetic Space Grotesk display headings paired with highly-legible Inter body fonts and JetBrains Mono for scheduling parameters.\n* **Cohesive Accents:** Features electric violet action items (`bg-violet-600`), secure emerald indicators (`text-emerald-400`), and a spinning vinyl launch icon.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 Architecture & Core Features\n\n#### 1. Header & Live Escrow Monitor\n* Displays active secured escrow funds aggregated across fully signed agreements.\n* Features a sandbox-active indicator, simulated active live sync badge, and dynamic user status tags depending on whether you are logged in as a planner or musician.\n\n#### 2. Dual-Role Persona Switcher\n* Located prominently at the top of the app, this sandbox-switcher allows you to seamlessly shift perspectives between an **Event Planner (Buyer)** and a **Live Musician (Seller)** to test and simulate end-to-end booking mechanics instantly.\n\n#### 3. View A: Event Planners & Organizers\n* **Metrics Dashboard:** Summarizes active open calls, pending candidate applications, and locked bookings.\n* **My Events Timeline:** Displays active managed listings, status badges, applicant counts, and a direct link to evaluate musicians.\n* **The Gig Creator:** An elegant multi-stage creation form with strict performance timeline windows (Soundcheck vs. Curfew), numerical talent fee budget parameters, and interactive chip lists for genres, instruments, and on-site backline gear provisions.\n\n#### 4. View B: Live Musicians & Sessionists\n* **Sleek Split-Pane Feed:** \n  - **Left Pane:** Displays scrollable cards with genre tags, requested instrument needs, and prominent talent-fee badges.\n  - **Right Pane:** Opens a comprehensive logistics sheet detailing soundcheck deadlines, clothing requirements, on-site backline gear arrays, and an interactive \"Apply with Profile\" slide-out cover letter tray.\n* **Multi-Band Availability Tracker:** An interactive grid of the week\'s days that lets musicians toggle availability status values (`available`, `busy`, `tentative`) with single-click cycles.\n* **Band Registry:** An active project manager where artists can register or remove bands they tour with.\n\n#### 5. Memorandum of Agreement (MoA) Contract Modal\n* Generates a legally protective performance agreement outlining schedules, compensation, and Force Majeure rules.\n* Integrates an electronic signature validation form with terms agreement checks, locking down the budget escrow status once approved by both roles.\n\n#### 6. Guided Sandbox walkthrough\n* Includes a step-by-step interactive walkthrough card on the footer helping users simulate the complete flow: creating a gig, applying as a musician, reviewing the candidate, signing the legal MoA, and securing funds in escrow. All state persists natively inside standard client-side `localStorage`."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 497566734
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
